---
import Layout from "../../../layouts/PageLayout.astro";

// Version BB-PRIVACY-v1.0, in force from 2026-11-02. Every statement about the app is
// backed by the BluBelt source (aunova/blubelt: the Android manifest, build.gradle.kts,
// blubelt-core transfer/store and the monetization crate). Change this page in the same
// release that changes what the app does.
const metadata = {
  title: "BluBelt Privacy Notice - Aunova",
  description:
    "How the BluBelt Android app handles data: your training log stays on your phone, the free version shows Google ads only if you agree, and the Pro purchase goes through Google Play.",
};
---

<Layout title={metadata.title} description={metadata.description}>
  <section class="legal-page">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="legal-header">
        <h1 class="legal-title">BluBelt Privacy Notice</h1>
        <p class="legal-updated">Last updated: November 2, 2026</p>
      </div>

      <div class="legal-content">
        <div class="legal-section">
          <h2>About this notice</h2>
          <p class="legal-intro">
            This notice covers one thing: the <strong>BluBelt</strong> app for Android
            (package <code>com.aunova.blubelt</code>). BluBelt logs your martial arts training and
            shows your progress on the belt system. This notice explains what happens to data when
            you use it. It covers both Aunova companies involved in the app.
          </p>
          <p>
            It does not cover the rest of aunova.net, which has its own
            <a href="/en/privacy">privacy policy</a>, or the BluBelt web app.
          </p>
          <p>The short version:</p>
          <ul class="legal-list">
            <li>Your training log stays on your phone. It is never sent to us or to anyone else.</li>
            <li>We have no account, no sign-in, no cloud, no analytics and no crash reporting of our own.</li>
            <li>
              The free version shows a Google ad only if you agree. If you say no, no ad is
              requested. If you say yes, Google's ad software collects data for the ad, and this
              notice says what.
            </li>
            <li>
              Neither Aunova company receives anything about you from the app. Aunova Technologies
              Ltd sees only Google's overall ad reports, such as how many ads were shown, which do
              not identify you.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="legal-section">
          <h2>Who is responsible, and how to reach us</h2>
          <p>Two Aunova companies are involved in BluBelt.</p>
          <p>
            <strong>Aunova OÜ</strong>, Ahtri tn 12, 15551 Tallinn, Harju maakond, Estonia
            (registry code 16837438, VAT: EE102670613). Aunova OÜ makes BluBelt and publishes it on
            Google Play. It decides how Google's ad software is built into the app and when the app
            asks for consent. It is also responsible for the purchase, the order records and the
            emails you send us.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Aunova Technologies Ltd</strong>, GA-00-SZ-L1-RT-164, Level 1, Gate Avenue -
            South Zone, Dubai International Financial Centre, Dubai, United Arab Emirates (DIFC
            licence CL13718). The ads in the free version run under Aunova Technologies Ltd's Google
            AdMob account. It sets up Google's consent form and receives the ad revenue.
          </p>
          <p>
            Both companies are responsible for the ads. You can contact either of them about the
            ads, and exercise your rights against either of them.
          </p>
          <p>
            You can reach both companies by email at
            <a href="mailto:chris@aunova.net">chris@aunova.net</a>, or by post at either address
            above.
          </p>
          <p>
            Neither company has appointed a Data Protection Officer. Data protection is handled
            internally, and the email address above reaches the person responsible for it at both
            companies.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="legal-section">
          <h2>Your training log stays on your phone</h2>
          <p>
            BluBelt saves what you enter in a database in the app's own storage on your phone: each
            training session (its date and the martial art) and your list of martial arts.
          </p>
          <ul class="legal-list">
            <li>It is never sent anywhere, to us or to anyone else. The app works offline.</li>
            <li>There is no account, no sign-in and no cloud copy.</li>
            <li>There is no analytics and no crash reporting of our own.</li>
            <li>
              <strong>Clear All Data</strong> in Settings deletes your sessions and resets the list
              of martial arts. Uninstalling the app deletes everything it saved.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Because we hold no copy, we cannot restore your log if you lose your phone or clear the
            app. Pro users can make their own backup, as described below.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="legal-section">
          <h2>Backup and restore (Pro)</h2>
          <p>
            With Pro, <strong>Export Data</strong> writes your sessions and martial arts list to a
            file, and <strong>Import Data</strong> reads such a file back. Both use Android's own
            file picker, so you choose where the file goes and which file to read. The app sees only
            the one file you pick.
          </p>
          <p>
            If you save the file to a cloud folder, such as Google Drive, that service stores it
            under its own privacy policy. We never receive the file.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="legal-section">
          <h2>Permissions</h2>
          <p>
            BluBelt never asks you to grant a permission. It needs none of the ones Android prompts
            for: no location, no contacts, no files, no phone state. The file picker for backup
            and restore works without one.
          </p>
          <p>
            The app does declare permissions that Android grants without asking. BluBelt's own code
            declares two of them; Google's ad, consent and billing software adds the rest. None of
            them is for anything the training log does:
          </p>
          <ul class="legal-list" data-android-permissions="android.permission.ACCESS_ADSERVICES_AD_ID android.permission.ACCESS_ADSERVICES_ATTRIBUTION android.permission.ACCESS_ADSERVICES_TOPICS android.permission.ACCESS_NETWORK_STATE android.permission.FOREGROUND_SERVICE android.permission.INTERNET android.permission.WAKE_LOCK com.android.vending.BILLING com.google.android.gms.permission.AD_ID">
            <li><strong>Internet</strong> and <strong>network state</strong>, to fetch an ad and the consent form.</li>
            <li><strong>Advertising ID</strong> and Android's <strong>ad services</strong> (ad ID, attribution and topics), because Google's ad software uses them.</li>
            <li><strong>Google Play Billing</strong>, for the Pro purchase.</li>
            <li><strong>Wake lock</strong> and <strong>foreground service</strong>, which Google's software declares for its own background work.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="legal-section">
          <h2>Ads in the free version</h2>
          <p>
            The free version can show one banner ad at the bottom of the screen, and only if you
            have agreed (see <strong>Consent for ads</strong>). The ad is the one part of the app
            that uses the network on its own. It comes from Google AdMob, through the Google Mobile
            Ads SDK, and runs under Aunova Technologies Ltd's AdMob account. If you have not agreed,
            no ad is requested.
          </p>
          <p>
            Once you have agreed, Google states that its Mobile Ads SDK collects and shares the
            following data automatically, for advertising, analytics and fraud prevention:
          </p>
          <ul class="legal-list">
            <li>
              <strong>IP address</strong>, which may be used to estimate the general location of
              your device.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Product interactions</strong>, such as app launches, taps and video views.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Diagnostic information</strong> about how the app and the SDK perform, such
              as app launch time, hang rate and energy usage.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Device and account identifiers</strong>: the Android advertising ID, the app
              set ID and, where applicable, other identifiers related to accounts signed in on the
              device.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Google states that this data is encrypted in transit. The source is Google's own
            <a href="https://developers.google.com/admob/android/privacy/play-data-disclosure">data
            disclosure for the Mobile Ads SDK</a>, which Google keeps up to date.
          </p>
          <p>
            Your training log is never part of the ad request. We do not pass Google any data of our
            own.
          </p>
          <p>
            Google uses the data it collects through its SDK under its own rules, and for AdMob it
            acts as an independent controller. Google may process this data outside your country,
            including in the United States. See
            <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google's privacy policy</a> and
            <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites">how Google uses
            information from sites or apps that use its services</a>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="legal-section">
          <h2>Consent for ads</h2>
          <p>
            In the free version, BluBelt asks for your consent through Google's consent form, from
            Google's User Messaging Platform. It includes a <strong>Do not consent</strong> option.
            <strong>No ad is requested unless you agree</strong>; if Google's form has not been shown
            to you, or you did not agree, the app requests no ads at all.
          </p>
          <p>If you say no, you see no ad and the app works exactly the same.</p>
          <p>
            <strong>What is saved on your phone.</strong> Google's consent tool saves your answer in
            BluBelt's own storage on your phone, in the standard format of the IAB Transparency and
            Consent Framework. It does this so that you are not asked every time you open the app,
            and so that Google's ad software can read what you allowed it to do. Your answer is not
            sent to us.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Changing your mind.</strong> Settings has a <strong>Privacy options</strong>
            button. It reopens Google's consent form, so you can change your answer or withdraw
            consent at any time. If you withdraw consent, you stop seeing the ad: from then on, no
            ad is requested. Withdrawing does not affect what happened before.
          </p>
          <p>You can also:</p>
          <ul class="legal-list">
            <li>
              <strong>Reset or delete your advertising ID</strong> with the ad ID controls in your
              phone's Android settings. This works for every app on the phone, not just BluBelt.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Buy Pro</strong>, described below. When Google Play confirms, as the app opens,
              that the purchase is on your Google account, BluBelt neither shows the consent form nor
              starts the ad software. If Google Play has not answered within about three seconds of
              the app opening, BluBelt treats that session as the free version. On such a start a
              buyer can still see the consent form and, after agreeing, the ad.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="legal-section">
          <h2>The Pro purchase</h2>
          <p>
            A one-time in-app purchase, <strong>Pro</strong>, removes the ad and unlocks backup and
            restore. "Restore purchases" in Settings brings it to another device signed in to the
            same Google account.
          </p>
          <p>
            The purchase runs through Google Play Billing. Google handles the payment. We never see
            your card or any other payment details.
          </p>
          <p>
            The app reads from Google Play only what it needs: whether this Google account owns
            Pro, and the purchase token Google uses to identify it. The app uses that token only to
            confirm the purchase to Google Play. It is not sent to us.
          </p>
          <p>
            Aunova OÜ, as the Google Play developer, can see an order record for each sale in Google
            Play Console. Google decides what it contains. It includes an order number, the date,
            the product, the price and tax, and the buyer's country, and in some cases the region
            and postcode. Aunova OÜ uses it only for its accounts.
          </p>
          <p>
            See the <a href="https://play.google.com/about/play-terms/">Google Play Terms of
            Service</a> and <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google's privacy
            policy</a>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="legal-section">
          <h2>Links that leave the app</h2>
          <p>
            Some things in BluBelt open a web address. Tapping one hands that address to your
            browser and leaves BluBelt. From there, the site you visit and its own privacy policy
            apply. Nothing from your training log goes with the link.
          </p>
          <ul class="legal-list">
            <li>
              <strong>The footer links</strong> open our Terms of Service and this notice on
              aunova.net.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>The banner ad</strong>, in the free version, opens whatever the advertiser's
              link points to. That link is not ours. What Google's ad software sends with the tap is
              covered by Google's policies above, and the advertiser's site has its own.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="legal-section">
          <h2>Our lawful basis</h2>
          <ul class="legal-list">
            <li>
              <strong>Your training log</strong> involves no processing of personal data by us. It
              stays on your phone and nothing leaves it.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Ads.</strong> Consent is the only basis, for every user. Aunova OÜ and Aunova
              Technologies Ltd rely on your consent for having the ad software store and read
              information on your phone, and collect your data and send it to Google: GDPR Article
              6(1)(a), and the consent rules for information stored on your device. For Aunova
              Technologies Ltd, this is also consent under the DIFC Data Protection Law 2020. No ad
              is requested without your consent, and you can withdraw it at any time (see
              <strong>Consent for ads</strong>). Google relies on its own lawful bases for what it
              does with the data afterwards; see Google's privacy policy.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>The purchase.</strong> Aunova OÜ handles the purchase status so that Pro
              works, because that is necessary to give you what you paid for: Article 6(1)(b).
              Keeping order records for its accounts is a legal obligation: Article 6(1)(c).
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>If you email us</strong>, the company you write to uses your message to answer
              it, on the basis of its legitimate interest in replying to you: Article 6(1)(f).
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p>Neither company makes any decision about you automatically.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="legal-section">
          <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
          <p>Neither Aunova company receives any data about you from the app, so neither keeps any.</p>
          <ul class="legal-list">
            <li>
              <strong>Your training log and your answer about ads</strong> stay on your phone until
              you clear them, clear the app's storage or uninstall the app.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Order records</strong> stay in Google Play Console. Aunova OÜ keeps them for
              as long as accounting law requires.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Emails you send us</strong> are kept until your question is settled, and then
              deleted.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            What Google keeps from its ad software and from Google Play is set by Google's
            policies, linked above.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="legal-section">
          <h2>Your rights</h2>
          <p>
            You have the following rights over any personal data we hold about you. Exercising any
            of them is free, and you never have to justify asking.
          </p>
          <ul class="legal-list">
            <li><strong>Access</strong> to the data and a copy of it. GDPR Article 15.</li>
            <li><strong>Rectification</strong> of inaccurate data. Article 16.</li>
            <li><strong>Erasure</strong> of your data. Article 17.</li>
            <li><strong>Restriction</strong> of what we do with it. Article 18.</li>
            <li><strong>Portability</strong> of the data you gave us. Article 20.</li>
            <li><strong>Objection</strong> to processing based on our legitimate interest. Article 21.</li>
            <li>
              <strong>Withdraw consent</strong> at any time, without affecting what was done before.
              Article 7(3). For ads, see <strong>Consent for ads</strong> above.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Complain</strong> to a supervisory authority, and seek a remedy in court. See
              below.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Because the app sends us nothing, we usually cannot link any data to you from BluBelt
            alone. Your training log is on your phone and under your control. The data the ad
            software collects is held by Google; to exercise your rights over it, use Google's own
            tools, described in <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google's privacy
            policy</a>.
          </p>
          <p>
            To ask us, email <a href="mailto:chris@aunova.net">chris@aunova.net</a> or write to
            either postal address above. For the ads, you can ask either company. You do not need to
            cite a law or fill in a form. We answer without undue delay and within one month of
            receiving your request. If a request is complex, or we receive many, we may extend that
            by up to two further months. If we do, we tell you within the first month, and why
            (GDPR Article 12(3)).
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="legal-section">
          <h2>Complaining to a supervisory authority</h2>
          <p>
            We would rather hear from you first, but you do not have to come to us at all. You can
            complain to the data protection authority of the country where you live, where you work,
            or where you think the problem happened, and you may seek a remedy in court.
          </p>
          <p>
            The authority for Aunova OÜ is the <strong>Estonian Data Protection
            Inspectorate</strong> (<em>Andmekaitse Inspektsioon</em>), Tatari 39, 10134 Tallinn,
            Estonia. Telephone +372 627 4135. Website <a href="https://www.aki.ee">www.aki.ee</a>.
          </p>
          <p>
            Aunova Technologies Ltd is also subject to the DIFC Data Protection Law 2020, and you
            can complain about it to the DIFC Commissioner of Data Protection, Dubai International
            Financial Centre, Dubai, United Arab Emirates. Website
            <a href="https://www.difc.com/business/registrars-and-commissioners/commissioner-of-data-protection">difc.com</a>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="legal-section">
          <h2>Children</h2>
          <p>BluBelt is not directed at children.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="legal-section">
          <h2>Changes to this notice</h2>
          <p>
            We update this notice when what the app does changes, and the version and date change
            with it. If a new version of the app sends anything new off the phone, this notice
            changes first.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="legal-section">
          <h2>Version and effective date</h2>
          <p>
            Version <strong>BB-PRIVACY-v1.0</strong>, in force from <strong>2 November 2026</strong>.
          </p>
          <p>This notice is pending review by qualified counsel. It is not legal advice.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .legal-page {
    padding: var(--space-3xl) 0 var(--space-5xl);
    min-height: calc(100vh - var(--header-height));
  }

  .legal-header {
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3xl);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-2xl);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .legal-title {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--color-primary), var(--color-secondary));
    background-size: 200% 200%;
    animation: gradient-shift 5s ease infinite;
  }

  .legal-updated {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .legal-content {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .legal-section {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2xl);
  }

  .legal-section h2 {
    font-size: 1.75rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .legal-intro {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .legal-section p {
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .legal-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: var(--space-md) 0;
  }

  .legal-list li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: var(--space-xl);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .legal-list li::before {
    content: "→";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: var(--color-primary);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .legal-list li strong {
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .legal-section a {
    color: var(--color-primary);
    text-decoration: underline;
    transition: opacity var(--transition-fast);
  }

  .legal-section a:hover {
    opacity: 0.8;
  }

  @keyframes gradient-shift {
    0%, 100% { background-position: 0% 50%; }
    50% { background-position: 100% 50%; }
  }

  /* Mobile styles */
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .legal-page {
      padding: var(--space-2xl) 0 var(--space-3xl);
    }

    .legal-header {
      margin-bottom: var(--space-2xl);
      padding-bottom: var(--space-xl);
    }

    .legal-section {
      margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);
    }

    .legal-section h2 {
      font-size: 1.5rem;
    }

    .legal-intro {
      font-size: 1rem;
    }
  }
</style>
